# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yong-Chao Wu et al. (2026). Machine-learned interatomic potential for large-scale simulations of the CrCoNi medium-entropy alloys.
#   Communications Materials. doi:10.1038/s43246-026-01245-3  arXiv:2603.25616v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2603.25616v1 (sha256 737ac0cf7e2bd7c8...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 625 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wu2026large.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the NEP model for the Cr-Co-Ni system trained with
# active learning, and the published CrCoNi MTP of Cao et al. (Ref. 24)
# re-evaluated as distributed, with the energy, force and stress RMSEs of
# Table I on the NEP training set, the MTP data set and an independent
# 84-structure validation set. EAM and MEAM potentials are classical and
# not encoded.

