###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The NEP's errors on the MTP data set have role null because the NEP training set includes part of it (TS-0, TS-3, TS-f); the MTP's errors on its own data set also have role null, since the paper does not state which of TS-0..TS-5 and TS-f were used to train it.
# - EAM1, EAM2 and MEAM errors (Table I) are classical potentials and not encoded. Simulation speed is shown only in Fig. 9 (relative throughput), so no timing is encoded. NEP hyperparameters are not stated in the text read.
# - Crystal, short-range-order, stacking-fault, melting and tensile properties (Table II, Figs. 2-8) are property comparisons.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wu2026large.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

